WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.320
Part 2. You will hear the Managing Director of a company called Stephenson's welcoming

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:13.000
a group of work experience students. First you have some time to look at questions 11

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.760
to 14.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:57.160
Good morning everyone and welcome to Stephenson's, one of the country's major manufacturers of

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:03.040
metal goods. Thank you for choosing us for your two weeks of work experience. My name

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:11.080
is Julia Simmons and since the beginning of this year I've been the Managing Director.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.400
Stephenson's is quite an old company. Like me, the founder, Ronald Stephenson, went into

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:23.480
the steel industry when he left school. That was in 1923. He set up this company when he

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:30.239
finished his apprenticeship in 1926, although he actually started making plans two years

00:01:30.239 --> 00:01:38.860
earlier in 1924. He was a very determined young man. Stephenson's long-term plan was

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:43.959
to manufacture components for the machine tools industry, although in fact that never

00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:50.720
came about, and for the automotive industry, that is cars and lorries. However, there was

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:56.839
a delay of five years before that happened, because shortly before the company went into

00:01:56.839 --> 00:02:03.400
production, Stephenson was given the opportunity to make goods for hospitals and other players

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:10.119
in the healthcare industry. So that's what we did for the first five years. Over the

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:16.600
years we've expanded the premises considerably. We were lucky that the site is big enough,

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:23.000
so moving to a new location has never been necessary. However, the layout is far from

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:29.679
ideal for modern machinery and production methods, so we intend to carry out major refurbishment

00:02:29.679 --> 00:02:36.600
of this site over the next five years. I'd better give you some idea of what you'll be

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:43.080
doing during your two weeks with us, so you know what to expect. Most mornings you'll

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:48.800
have a presentation from one of the managers to learn about their department, starting

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:55.960
this morning with research and development, and you'll all spend some time in each department

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:01.440
observing what's going on and talking to people, as long as you don't stop them from doing

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:07.679
their work altogether. In the past, a teacher from your school has come in at the end of

00:03:07.679 --> 00:03:13.160
each week to find out how the group were getting on, but your school isn't able to

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:21.919
arrange that this year. Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look

00:03:21.919 --> 00:03:24.119
at questions 15 to 20.

00:03:37.679 --> 00:04:07.639
OK, now I'll briefly help you to orientate yourselves around the site. As you can see,

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:15.080
we're in the reception area, which we try to make attractive and welcoming to visitors.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:20.359
There's a corridor running left from here, and if you go along that, the door facing

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:26.399
you at the end is the entrance to the coffee room. This looks out onto the main road on

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:33.600
one side and some trees on the other, and that'll be where you meet each morning. The

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:40.480
factory is the very big room on the far side of the site. Next to it is the warehouse,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:46.480
which can be accessed by lorries going up the road to the turning area at the end. You

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:51.839
can get to the warehouse by crossing to the far side of the courtyard, and then the door

00:04:51.839 --> 00:04:58.760
is on your right. Somewhere you'll be keen to find is the staff canteen. This is right

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:05.799
next to reception. I can confidently say that the food's very good, but the view isn't.

00:05:05.799 --> 00:05:11.239
The windows on one side look onto a corridor and courtyard, which aren't very attractive

00:05:11.239 --> 00:05:19.279
at all, and on the other onto the access road, which isn't much better. You'll be using the

00:05:19.279 --> 00:05:25.359
meeting room quite often, and you'll find it by walking along the corridor to the left

00:05:25.359 --> 00:05:32.359
of the courtyard and continuing along it to the end. The meeting room is the last one

00:05:32.359 --> 00:05:39.640
on the right, and I'm afraid there's no natural daylight in the room. Then you'll need to

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:45.440
know where some of the offices are. The human resources department is at the front of this

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:51.640
building, so you head to the left along the corridor from reception, and it's the second

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:58.720
room you come to. It looks out onto the main road. And finally the boardroom, where you'll

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:05.600
be meeting sometimes. That has quite a pleasant view, as it looks out onto the trees. Go along

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:11.760
the corridor past the courtyard, right to the end. The boardroom is on the left, next

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:26.839
to the factory. Okay now, are there any questions before we move on?

